From: MaSi <noreply@masi.local>
Subject: [PATCH] PM: hex-dump the SDAM slot after a stuck resume

The text form stops at the first zero, so a surviving prefix hides the
rest of the driver name.

---
--- a/drivers/base/power/main.c
+++ b/drivers/base/power/main.c
@@ -755,6 +755,9 @@
 			return;
 		}
 		pr_emerg("previous DPM timeout: %s\n", buf + off + 2);
+		print_hex_dump(KERN_EMERG, "PM: sdam-slot ",
+			       DUMP_PREFIX_OFFSET, 16, 1,
+			       buf + off, len, true);
 		memset(buf + off, 0, len);
 		regmap_bulk_write(map, DPM_STUCK_SDAM_REG + off, buf + off, len);
 		return;
